<title>GERMANY: Issing-Germany risks missing EMU criteria in 96.</title>
<headline>Issing-Germany risks missing EMU criteria in 96.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG, Germany 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank chief economist Otmar Issing said on Monday that Germany was in danger of missing the debt and deficit criteria this year that are necessary to join Europe's planned monetary union.</p>
<p>&quot;There is a danger that Germany will again clearly miss the three percent deficit criteria this year and recently it has also exceeded the 60 percent debt target,&quot; Issing told a group of bankers.</p>
<p>The Maastricht Treaty on European Economic and Monetary Union must not allow their budget deficits to exceed three percent of gross domestic product and total public debt must not exceed 60 percent of gross domestic product.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
